# .gitignore
#
# Ignore rules for mega_archive_service.
#
# Sections:
#   1. Local environment and credentials
#   2. Python build artefacts
#   3. Storage — Job 1 archive and Job 2 runtime state
#   4. Logs and runtime output
#   5. Test artefacts
#   6. Editor / OS noise
#   7. Project-specific dev scratch files
#
# Design note on storage/
# -----------------------
# ``storage/`` is NOT blanket-ignored at the top level. Only its two
# managed subtrees are ignored:
#
#   storage/downloads/   Job 1 download target (the ZIP)
#   storage/mega/        Job 1 extraction target + Job 2 runtime state
#
# The .gitkeep exceptions keep the empty parent directories in the repo
# so a fresh clone has the same skeleton. Everything the running service
# produces stays out of git.
#
# Transient swap directories created by archive_service.py during a
# refresh — ``storage/.mega.backup`` and ``storage/.mega-stage-*`` — live
# directly under ``storage/``, not under either managed subtree, so they
# need their own rule (``storage/.mega*``).

# ---------- 1. Local environment and credentials ----------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
credentials.json
secrets.json
secrets.yaml

# ---------- 2. Python ----------
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
myenv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
pip-wheel-metadata/
.eggs/

# ---------- 3. Storage — Job 1 archive and Job 2 runtime state ----------
#
# Job 1 writes to storage/downloads/ (the ZIP) and storage/mega/ (the
# extracted tree). Job 2 persists state to storage/mega/_ema_state/ and
# storage/mega/{index,<underlying>}/ema_crosses.json. None of these are
# source — the .gitkeep exceptions keep the empty parent directories in
# the repo.
storage/downloads/*
!storage/downloads/.gitkeep
storage/mega/*
!storage/mega/.gitkeep

# Explicit subtrees documented here for clarity — covered by the
# wildcards above, listed so intent is obvious at a glance.
storage/mega/_ema_state/
storage/mega/index/
storage/mega/nifty/
storage/mega/sensex/
storage/mega/all_instruments.json

# Transient swap directories during a MEGA refresh. archive_service.py
# creates .mega.backup and .mega-stage-* directly under storage/ (same
# filesystem as storage/mega/ so the rename is atomic).
storage/.mega*

# ---------- 4. Logs and runtime output ----------
logs/
logs_*/
test_logs/
temp/
data/
meta_data/
downloads/
output/
*.pid
*.log
*.log.*
*.jsonl
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*

# ---------- 5. Test artefacts ----------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
*.cover

# ---------- 6. Editor / OS noise ----------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------- 7. Project-specific dev scratch files ----------
combined_output.txt
files.txt
project_structure.txt
storage